96d287359ebde7ad0f3e5b6bc32be46500db9c3a5e1b5f561f32469db01","event_uuid":"f6a0c58c-db5e-4d0c-ac8d-b67ec84b9f32","position":{"commit_sha":"a86afc0daa0f6a32947918cf37c1e0ad591569ee","position":"1787859277224239156-f6a0c58c-db5e-4d0c-ac8d-b67ec84b9f32"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e51de44e1469e8b73621c2deeac1df1367386bd6b1567781f051547db4ac3f8b","event_uuid":"b235bdcb-e346-418c-8b44-95642e40cb28","position":{"commit_sha":"287359e8c579f9ca42d98e001ce3c790debf0350","position":"1787859279925555488-b235bdcb-e346-418c-8b44-95642e40cb28"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"deae4dcc7b66f1a277424d072084887f7e78447fe7d25d9bd411227c77c573e2","event_uuid":"0b9d6040-8d90-4f8f-8758-f9c4ff9727df","position":{"commit_sha":"237197591d0a382605f899bbc728f4efc2f84e40","position":"1787859282609230395-0b9d6040-8d90-4f8f-8758-f9c4ff9727df"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Additional evidence from lead-unpleasing-kitten: `test_ran_and_skipped_coexist_in_one_run` says its skipped record represents absent scc/lizard, but on this host scc 3.7.0 is present and the test still passes because unrelated inapplicable detectors contribute skipped records. Therefore it does not prove metric present or metric absent behavior. The deterministic metric-absence nodes do force `_METRIC_CANDIDATES`, so absence accounting remains covered; the new positive metric oracle must assert the backend and detector id explicitly.","timestamp":1786911603437863001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## PHASE 1 EXIT — proven root cause (rebar-debug fast path)\n\nRuntime reproduction on scc 3.7.0 traced the actual production call in `src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke`:\n\n- argv executed: `['/opt/homebrew/bin/scc', '--format', 'json', '.']`\n- parsed `Files` counts: 27 language groups, all zero\n- `_run_metric` result: `[]`, even though the repository contains files above the shipped 800-code-line cutoff\n- counterfactual with the same binary and input plus `--by-file`: 2,912 per-file entries, 29 with `Code > 800`\n\nConfirmed root cause: `_metric_invoke` omits scc's `--by-file` option at `engine_b_backends.py:376`. scc therefore emits only language summaries with empty `Files` arrays. `_scc_files` at lines 429-436 correctly consumes only per-file entries and consequently yields none; the threshold loop at lines 412-425 never executes and no metric match can be emitted. The only plausible alternative—that parsing or threshold comparison rejects otherwise-present entries—is ruled out by passing the same binary's `--by-file` JSON through `_scc_files`, which produced the expected 2,912 entries and 29 over-cutoff candidates.\n\nLegitimacy: `defect`. `src/rebar/grounding/detectors/builtin/smell_metric_oversize.yaml` authoritatively says `oversize_loc` flags files over a LOC cutoff, while `engine_b_backends.py:339-344` promises a present metric binary emits a match per file over the cutoff. Current behavior violates both contracts. Closed bug `rapid-cuboid-velvetcrab` independently established the same scc output contract for the metrics adapter and explicitly identified grounding `_scc_files` as a separate consumer.\n\nCaller-dependency gate: expected post-fix behavior is that a present scc invocation yields normalized matches for every returned file whose `Code` exceeds the configured cutoff, while below-cutoff files and all existing fail-open paths remain unchanged. The bounded caller sweep found `_metric_invoke` called only by `_run_metric`; that runner is dispatched through Engine B scan and then the grounding oracle. These callers consume evidence records and contractually expect matches, not an empty result. No behavioral dependency on the defect exists.\n\nFast-path criteria: deterministic reproduction, one directly observed mechanism, and a one-argument localized/reversible repair all hold. Phase 2 is unlocked after current plan review.","timestamp":1786913144351601001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## PHASE 2 REPORT — rebar-debug complete; Gerrit gates pending\n\n**Problem:** the present scc grounding metric backend could never emit per-file oversize matches.\n\n**Proven root cause:** `src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke` invoked `scc --format json <repo>` without `--by-file`. scc 3.7.0 returned language summaries whose `Files` arrays were empty; `_scc_files` therefore yielded no entries and the threshold loop never ran.\n\n**Proof:** a runtime trace through `_run_metric` captured the exact argv, 27 zero-length `Files` arrays, and `records=[]`. The same binary/repository with `--by-file` returned 2,912 entries, including 29 with `Code > 800`, ruling out parser and threshold alternatives.\n\n**Test/TDD:** `tests/unit/grounding/test_engine_b.py::test_metric_backend_requests_per_file_json_and_emits_only_over_cutoff` crosses `_run_metric -> _metric_invoke -> harness boundary -> JSON parser -> _scc_files -> ev.match` with an argv-faithful scc fake. Its preconditions prove 801- and 800-line inputs. In final form it was collected and observed RED first (`0 != 1` matches), physically removed from the worktree, and withheld from the fixer. The fixer saw only the RCA/reproduction/contract card. Restored afterward, it was GREEN on the first repair attempt. Defect-seeded mutation (remove `--by-file`) returned it to the same RED; restoring the fix returned GREEN. The refactoring litmus removed irrelevant flag-order coupling, then the revised final oracle was re-proven RED without the fix and GREEN with it. Timeout, nonzero exit, invalid JSON, and absent-tool fail-open paths are covered and green.\n\n**Fix:** commit `0cc74619ec405ad2927b7ad451aed416dcc664b5` adds the one required scc argument; no threshold, `Code` field, evidence shape, or failure behavior changed. Repair attempts: 1.\n\n**Scope/safety:** bounded caller sweep found `_metric_invoke` called only by `_run_metric`; Engine B scan/oracle consumers expect evidence matches and none relies on the empty result. This restores the built-in detector contract, creates no API or capability, adds no dependency, and weakens no test. Signed plan-review PASS was current before Phase 2.\n\n**Verification:** focused held-out/failure coverage 5 passed; focused grounding cohort passed; `make check` passed (ruff, format, complexity, workflow checks, mypy); CI-equivalent default suite passed `13,535 passed, 52 skipped` in 797.44s. Original live `_run_metric(Path(\".\"))` now emits 29 normalized matches, including real over-800 files.\n\n**Sibling sweeps:** construct sweep found exactly two production consumers that parse scc `Files`: grounding (fixed here) and `src/rebar/metrics/analyzers/scc_loc.py`, which already has the documented `--by-file` requirement from closed bug rapid-cuboid-velvetcrab. No unfixed construct sibling. Parity rule: per-file scc consumers must explicitly request per-file JSON. CLI/MCP have no independent metric implementation; library grounding oracle, code review, plan review, and criterion preview all route through shared Engine B; the separate metrics analyzer is already correct; no mirror direction applies. No MISSING surface.\n\n**Residual warning dispositions:** existing open owners: `unamicable-exuberant-chupacabra` (enrich-drain >20ms) and `ferrety-crippling-dairycow` (Pydantic unresolved lifespan). Newly filed+linked for dedicated debug: `treelike-unamusing-grosbeak` (Python 3.14 tar filter), `stumpy-cinnabar-basenji` (multithreaded fork/deadlock warning), `dragonish-sylphic-sheep` (OpenAI prefix v2 semantic change; decision brief recorded, no implementation pending approval), and `socialized-exclusive-mouse` (Pydantic event-loop warning; handed to the separate RP-01 session).\n\n**Landing:** Gerrit 1829, patch set 1. Local code-review capability is disabled; authoritative LLM-Review and Verified gates are running. Ticket remains in_progress until both are +1, the change is submitted, and origin/main contains the merge.","timestamp":1786915180763977001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## LANDED AND CLOSED\n\nGerrit change 1829 patch set 1 earned `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, and had zero unresolved comments. CI run 31973003971 completed SUCCESS across all 17 jobs. Plain Gerrit Submit merged commit `0cc74619ec405ad2927b7ad451aed416dcc664b5`; both `gerrit/main` and the GitHub mirror `origin/main` now point at that SHA.\n\nThe refreshed completion verifier returned signed PASS against the exact merged SHA with every acceptance criterion met. The ticket closed as class `preexisting` without force and recorded a signed completion signature.","timestamp":1786916918167518001}],"created_at":1786910974260071001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"053f0e02-24db-4287-981a-0c18eccb0d43","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7da8-9d47-9604-4257"},{"link_uuid":"ccb7113b-9be5-4af5-9781-080c8b23455a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"01d4-1263-460a-416d"},{"link_uuid":"7461a94d-d203-44c3-a1e1-fd07b41582ed","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1154-2a8e-48f9-4e16"},{"link_uuid":"2d37ebc5-7c87-4729-9c01-9a5464b1b98c","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"25bf-a5a2-6bc2-4c5c"}],"description":"## Context\nThe Engine B metric backend parses per-file entries from scc JSON, but `_metric_invoke` invokes `scc --format json <repo>` without `--by-file`. With maintained scc 3.7.0, the language summary includes `Files: []` unless `--by-file` is requested. Therefore a present scc process can run successfully while `rebar.builtin.smell.metric-oversize` sees no files and can never emit its documented over-800-LOC matches.\n\nThe analogous code-health adapter defect was fixed by closed bug rapid-cuboid-velvetcrab. The grounding backend `_scc_files` is a separate, previously unaudited consumer of the same scc JSON shape. Current coverage-reconstruction tests use a 50-LOC fixture or force tool absence, so they do not exercise the positive metric threshold path.\n\n## Reproduction\n- Run `scc --format json tests/unit/grounding` and inspect each language `Files` array: it is empty.\n- Compare with `scc --by-file --format json tests/unit/grounding`: per-file entries are present.\n- Inspect `src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke`: its command omits `--by-file` while `_scc_files` depends on `Files`.\n\n## Plan\n- Use rebar-debug to reproduce with a real scc binary and an over-800-code-line fixture, then prove the exact argv cause before editing.\n- Add a physically withheld RED oracle that observes a real or argv-faithful scc boundary and only produces per-file entries when `--by-file` is present.\n- Correct the grounding metric invocation without changing the existing `Code` field, thresholds, or fail-open semantics.\n- Add positive match, below-threshold no-match, invalid-output, nonzero-exit, and tool-absent coverage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A present scc run over a file above the configured LOC threshold emits a normalized metric match for that file.\n- [x] A present scc run below the threshold emits no fabricated match.\n- [x] The scc command requests per-file JSON explicitly; checked by an argv-sensitive test.\n- [x] Tool absence, timeout/nonzero failure, and invalid JSON remain fail-open evidence outcomes.\n- [x] The focused grounding backend tests pass with the held-out exact-defect oracle.\n\n## Verification\n- Run the focused grounding metric tests with the worktree virtualenv.\n- Run the repository lint and typecheck gates.\n- Run the default test suite before landing through Gerrit.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py","reason":"correct scc argv to request per-file JSON"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_engine_b.py","reason":"add metric present-path and argv-sensitive regression coverage"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","01d4-1263-460a-416d"],["relates_to","1154-2a8e-48f9-4e16"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5842de68-ae36-4f2a-9425-838543e85c06","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["grounding","bug","scc"],"ticket_id":"0024-fa99-d5bb-49bc","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Grounding metric detector omits scc --by-file and can never emit file matches","verify_commands":[],"workflow_runs":{"1787859271612944062-8439d43960754aebafcbfcfe508a990b":{"error":"step 'triggers' failed: input 'plan' is not set for this run","run_id":"1787859271612944062-8439d43960754aebafcbfcfe508a990b","status":"failed","terminal_step":"decide","workflow_name":"review_skeleton"}},"workflow_steps":{"1787859271612944062-8439d43960754aebafcbfcfe508a990b":{"triggers":{"captured":{"now_ns":1787859279923520776,"seed":838241557,"uuid":"019d778d20d7476c9f74b2daba42bbca"},"error":"input 'plan' is not set for this run","frame_key":"triggers","iteration":null,"kind":"scripted","outputs":{},"ru